    "body": "With https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/6655 and https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/6656 we almost have the spec matching [the cases I see in Chromium codesearch](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/bindings/core/v8/v8_binding_for_core.h;l=417;drc=f9ebf0deab3efad7c0db6843af187bb36f0ccb4c;bpv=1;bpt=1?q=EnteredDOMWindow&ss=chromium%2Fchromium%2Fsrc), i.e. `Location`, `document.open()`/`document.write()`, and `window.open()`.\r\n\r\nWhat remains is the spec uses the entry settings object for hyperlink downloading, which needs to be rebased on top of navigation in general.",
